# Settings for `docker compose` (copy to .env, fill every value, never commit it). See docs/DEPLOYMENT.md.
# Every variable below is also passed to the backend container.

# --- database (letters and digits only in the passwords: they are placed inside a URL) ---
DB_NAME=vidhi
MONGO_ROOT_USER=root
MONGO_ROOT_PASSWORD=
MONGO_APP_USER=vidhi_app
MONGO_APP_PASSWORD=

# --- public address (HTTPS, as users will see it) ---
APP_URL=https://app.example.in
CORS_ORIGINS=https://app.example.in
APP_TZ=Asia/Kolkata
# The host name only (no https://). The HTTPS proxy gets and renews a certificate for it automatically. Its DNS record must already point at this server.
DOMAIN=app.example.in

# --- Backups (compose service `backup`) ---
# Encrypted backups of the whole database, made every BACKUP_EVERY_HOURS and kept BACKUP_KEEP_DAYS days in ./backups. The passphrase is NOT here:
# it is the file ./secrets/backup_passphrase (see docs/hosting-runbook.md). Copy the backups OFF this server too.
BACKUP_EVERY_HOURS=24
BACKUP_KEEP_DAYS=30
# Restore drill (backend/tools/restore_drill.py): the address of a scratch MongoDB to restore the newest backup into. Empty means it uses MONGO_URL. It creates and drops a throwaway database, never the live one.
RESTORE_DRILL_MONGO_URL=
# The list of erased things (kinds and ids only) that survives a restore; tools/reapply_erasures.py reads it. Empty means no list. docker-compose.yml sets it to /backups/erasures.jsonl.
ERASURE_LEDGER_FILE=
# Default retention. These periods are choices made in code, not legal advice: an advocate must confirm them. 0 turns a period off; an empty or invalid value means the built-in default.
# Closed matters and resolved recovery cases: days after closing before they are deleted (after 30 days of warning to the owners), for organisations that did not choose their own number.
# Empty or 0 means no platform default (nothing is deleted unless the organisation chose a period). At least 30.
DEFAULT_RETENTION_DAYS_AFTER_CLOSE=
# The platform's own records, deleted this many days after they were made.
EMAIL_LOG_DAYS=365
SUPPORT_TICKET_DAYS=365
USAGE_EVENT_DAYS=400
AUDIT_EVENT_DAYS=730
# Questions and answers typed straight into Ask, outside any matter.
RESEARCH_NO_MATTER_DAYS=90

# --- Google Gemini ---
GEMINI_API_KEY=
GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-3.8-flash
# The light model used on the FREE plan (Pro uses GEMINI_MODEL)
GEMINI_FREE_MODEL=gemini-3.5-flash-lite
# --- Groq (OpenAI-compatible; fast fall-back, and the free plan's second model) ---
GROQ_API_KEY=
GROQ_MODEL=openai/gpt-oss-120b
GROQ_FREE_MODEL=openai/gpt-oss-20b
# --- NVIDIA hosted models (text only, last in the fallback order). Models: the names listed for your key at integrate.api.nvidia.com/v1/models ---
NVIDIA_API_KEY=
# --- Mistral and Z.ai (text only, after Groq and before NVIDIA in the fallback order) ---
MISTRAL_API_KEY=
MISTRAL_MODEL=mistral-small-latest
ZAI_API_KEY=
ZAI_MODEL=glm-4.5-flash
NVIDIA_MODEL=mistralai/mistral-large-4-1t-a52b
# --- OpenRouter: reaches Claude Sonnet / Haiku with one key when there is no Anthropic key ---
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
OPENROUTER_SONNET_MODEL=anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5
OPENROUTER_HAIKU_MODEL=anthropic/claude-haiku-5.5
# --- Anthropic Claude (Sonnet + Haiku). Optional: with only one provider's key, only that provider is used ---
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# CLAUDE_API_KEY= (accepted as the same setting as ANTHROPIC_API_KEY; ANTHROPIC_API_KEY wins if both are set)
CLAUDE_API_KEY=
ANTHROPIC_SONNET_MODEL=
ANTHROPIC_HAIKU_MODEL=
# --- Which model answers first (comma list of gemini,sonnet,haiku; the next one is used if one fails) ---
# The app picks by task (quick extraction/research: haiku; synthesis, contracts, notices: sonnet; images, long input: gemini).
# Override one task with AI_ROUTE_<TASK>, e.g. AI_ROUTE_SYNTHESIZE=sonnet,gemini; AI_ROUTE overrides everything
AI_ROUTE=
AI_ROUTE_RESEARCH=
# Cheap-draft / strong-final profile (NOT the default; switch only after scripts/route_compare.py shows equal or better quality):
#   AI_ROUTE_RESEARCH=sonnet,gemini,haiku   (the final answer)   AI_ROUTE_CLAIM_CHECK=sonnet,gemini,haiku   (the claim check)
#   easy steps stay cheap by default: AI_ROUTE_ANALYZE_EVIDENCE / AI_ROUTE_RECOVERY_EXTRACT (haiku first), translate-query / classify / query-rewrite (light or local model)
AI_ROUTE_CLAIM_CHECK=
# Free plan: light models only, in this order (never Claude).
AI_ROUTE_FREE=gemini,groq
# --- Plans (Legal Intelligence). Recovery is free for everyone. ---
FREE_AI_PER_DAY=5
FREE_AI_PLATFORM_PER_DAY=3000
KNOWLEDGE_MAX_PRIVATE_DOCS=200
KNOWLEDGE_MAX_PRIVATE_CHARS=20000000
PRO_AI_PER_DAY=500
FREE_CONTEXT_CHARS=12000

# --- Stripe: Pro is a MONTHLY subscription; the price is configuration, never client input ---
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=
STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
# --- Razorpay (UPI, cards, netbanking, monthly auto-pay; best for customers in India). Keys: Dashboard > Account & Settings > API keys.
# Webhook: Dashboard > Webhooks > add https://YOUR-DOMAIN/api/webhook/razorpay, tick the subscription.* events, set a secret and put it below.
# --- Sign in with Google: Google Cloud Console > APIs & Services > Credentials > OAuth client (Web). Redirect URI: <APP_URL>/api/auth/google/callback
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
# --- Microsoft 365 connection (Outlook mail, OneDrive and SharePoint files; read-only, each person's own account). Microsoft Entra ID > App registrations. Redirect URI: <APP_URL>/api/connectors/microsoft/callback
# Steps: docs/MICROSOFT_AND_IMANAGE_SETUP.md. MS_TENANT_ID is optional (one firm's directory ID; empty accepts any work or school account). MS_REDIRECT_URI only if the address differs.
MS_CLIENT_ID=
MS_CLIENT_SECRET=
MS_TENANT_ID=
MS_REDIRECT_URI=
# --- Voice. ElevenLabs: speech to text (Scribe) and natural multilingual voices. Without it, speech to text uses Gemini and listening uses the browser's own voice.
ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=
ELEVENLABS_VOICE_ID=
# STT_PROVIDER=elevenlabs or gemini (which to try first)
# --- SendGrid (alternative to Resend). Webhook: Settings > Mail Settings > Event Webhook > URL <APP_URL>/api/webhooks/sendgrid, enable Signed Event Webhook and paste its public key below.
# EMAIL_PROVIDER=resend or sendgrid (default: Resend if its key is set)
SENDGRID_API_KEY=
SENDGRID_WEBHOOK_PUBLIC_KEY=
# --- Twilio: opt-in SMS / WhatsApp alerts to the account owner's own verified phone (never to customers). Inbound webhook: <APP_URL>/api/webhooks/twilio
TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID=
TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN=
# Preferred instead of the auth token for sending: a Twilio API key (Console > Account > API keys). The auth token is still needed to verify inbound STOP replies.
TWILIO_API_KEY_SID=
TWILIO_API_KEY_SECRET=
TWILIO_FROM=
TWILIO_WHATSAPP_FROM=
# --- PayPal (customers outside India, billed in US dollars). Create a Subscriptions-enabled app + a webhook (URL <APP_URL>/api/webhook/paypal, events BILLING.SUBSCRIPTION.* and PAYMENT.SALE.COMPLETED).
# PayPal is offered only when PRO_PRICE_USD (your monthly dollar price) is set. PAYPAL_ENV=sandbox until you go live, then live.
PAYPAL_CLIENT_ID=
PAYPAL_CLIENT_SECRET=
PAYPAL_WEBHOOK_ID=
PAYPAL_ENV=sandbox
PRO_PRICE_USD=
# --- Rare illustrations (Gemini image model). OFF unless true. Pro only, capped per organisation per month, always labelled AI-generated.
IMAGE_GEN_ENABLED=false
IMAGE_MONTHLY_CAP=3
# IMAGE_MODEL=  (default in lib/imagegen.py; check Google's current image model list)
# --- Monthly AI spending cap (enforced in the backend). Alert at AI_ALERT_PERCENT to OWNER_ALERT_EMAIL; at 100% AI features pause until next month (IST).
AI_MONTHLY_CAP_INR=20000
# Daily caps (IST day), enforced in the backend, each with its own clear message. Set from what you are willing to spend and from the real ledger (scripts/cost_report.py).
# The numbers below are ASSUMED from docs/VIDHI_COST_MODEL.md (a Pro research answer about 4 rupees, a whole-matter synthesis about 34, a free-plan question about 1). 0 turns a cap off.
# Everyone together: three times the monthly average.
AI_DAILY_CAP_INR=2000
# All free-plan accounts together: they can never use up the day's money that Pro customers pay for.
AI_FREE_DAILY_CAP_INR=500
# One Pro person (Rs 1,999 a month), like Claude's plans: a rolling window of a few hours, a day, a week and the month, in rupees of AI cost.
# The month is at most half of the price; the week is a quarter of the month; the day about two sevenths of the week; the window two thirds of a day.
AI_WINDOW_HOURS=5
AI_USER_WINDOW_CAP_INR=40
AI_USER_DAILY_CAP_INR=60
AI_USER_WEEKLY_CAP_INR=200
AI_USER_MONTHLY_CAP_INR=800
# One free-plan person (the free plan allows 5 requests a day).
AI_FREE_USER_DAILY_CAP_INR=15
AI_ALERT_PERCENT=80
OWNER_ALERT_EMAIL=
# Price assumptions: the defaults are cautious placeholders. Put each provider's REAL current price (USD per million tokens, [input, output]) here.
# AI_PRICES_JSON={"sonnet": [2, 10]}   # only to override the built-in per-model prices (lib/aibudget.py MODEL_PRICES, read from the providers' pages on 2026-10-31)
# AI_USD_INR=97   # set to the current RBI reference rate; the built-in 97 is a cautious value, not today's rate
# --- Your genuine business details for the legal pages. Leave empty until you have them: the pages show a visible 'not configured yet' marker. NEVER invent values.
BUSINESS_LEGAL_NAME=
BUSINESS_REGISTERED_ADDRESS=
BUSINESS_REGISTRATION_NUMBER=
# Only if the business is GST-registered (the app checks the format only, it cannot verify registration):
BUSINESS_GSTIN=
GRIEVANCE_OFFICER_NAME=
GRIEVANCE_OFFICER_EMAIL=
GRIEVANCE_OFFICER_ADDRESS=
PRIVACY_CONTACT_EMAIL=
SUPPORT_EMAIL=
# Optional: leave empty until there is a genuine business WhatsApp number
SUPPORT_WHATSAPP=
# Our own target for answering a data request (not a legal deadline)
DATA_REQUEST_RESPONSE_DAYS=30
# --- Operator tools. PLATFORM_ADMIN_EMAILS: who may open the admin console (confirmed email AND two-step sign-in required). Comma separated.
PLATFORM_ADMIN_EMAILS=
# Error tracking (optional). Messages are scrubbed of personal details before sending. Leave empty to keep it off.
SENTRY_DSN=
SENTRY_ENVIRONMENT=production
# Who is told when the site is down (informational: the monitor itself is set up in GitHub Actions or an uptime service)
UPTIME_ALERT_CONTACT=
# --- Bot protection on signup: Cloudflare Turnstile (free). dash.cloudflare.com > Turnstile > add a site. Site key is public, secret key stays here. Without it only a weak fallback applies.
TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=
TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY=
# Owners/admins of a team must use two-step sign-in after this many days of notice (set TWO_STEP_FOR_TEAMS=false only to turn the rule off)
TWO_STEP_GRACE_DAYS=7
RAZORPAY_KEY_ID=
RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET=
RAZORPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
# Optional: which payment methods to offer and in what order, e.g. razorpay,stripe (default: every one whose keys are set)
PAYMENT_PROVIDERS=
PRO_PRICE_AMOUNT=1999
PRO_PRICE_CURRENCY=inr

# --- Resend ---
RESEND_API_KEY=
EMAIL_FROM=
EMAIL_REPLY_TO=
RESEND_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# --- scheduler + signed links: generate each with e.g.  python -c "import secrets; print(secrets.token_urlsafe(48))"
WEBHOOK_CRON_SECRET=
LINK_SECRET=
# Encrypts uploaded files at rest (AES-256-GCM). One or more keys, comma-separated; the first encrypts, all can read (rotation).
# Generate:  python -c "import base64,os; print(base64.urlsafe_b64encode(os.urandom(32)).decode())"
# Keep a copy somewhere safe: a lost key means the encrypted files cannot be opened. Empty = files are stored unencrypted.
DATA_ENCRYPTION_KEY=

# --- Optional tuning and aliases (all have sensible defaults) ---
# STRIPE_API_KEY=  (accepted as an alias of STRIPE_SECRET_KEY)
# GOOGLE_REDIRECT_URI=  (only if it differs from <APP_URL>/api/auth/google/callback)
# TWILIO_WEBHOOK_URL=  (only if the public address Twilio calls differs from <APP_URL>/api/webhooks/twilio; used to verify signatures)
# Defaults for these models are in lib/voice.py; check ElevenLabs' current model list:
# ELEVENLABS_STT_MODEL=
# ELEVENLABS_TTS_MODEL=
# AI_LONG_PROMPT_CHARS=120000  (above this many characters Gemini, with the longest context, is tried first)
# Placeholder prices for the spend cap; set the real ones:
# AI_PRICE_TTS_PER_1K_CHARS_USD=0.30
# AI_PRICE_STT_PER_MIN_USD=0.40
# AI_PRICE_IMAGE_USD=0.08
# TWO_STEP_FOR_TEAMS=true
# APP_VERSION=  (a release label sent with error reports, e.g. a git commit id)
# --- Browser notifications for saved dates (hearings, filing dates). Make the key once: python scripts/make-vapid-keys.py. Keep it secret; changing it makes every browser subscribe again.
VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=
# Contact the push services may use (default: SUPPORT_EMAIL, else PRIVACY_CONTACT_EMAIL):
# VAPID_SUBJECT=mailto:you@example.com
# --- Lawyer directory (public listing + consultation requests). OFF until a lawyer has confirmed it is permitted for your lawyers to be listed this way: docs/DIRECTORY.md
DIRECTORY_ENABLED=false
# Legal Recovery: false (default) = the small free helper (questions, free portal first, notice to download or copy, three dates). true = also email sending, escalation steps and the full case page.
# Legal Recovery is NOT part of the app unless this is true (owner, 2026-11-15). The code and saved cases stay; true brings everything back.
RECOVERY_ENABLED=false
RECOVERY_FULL_FLOW=false
# Meaning-based search over the law provisions (lib/embeddings.py): OFF by default. To use it: pip packages onnxruntime, tokenizers, numpy (in requirements.txt); put the model folder of
# intfloat/multilingual-e5-small (MIT licence; needs onnx/model.onnx and tokenizer.json) somewhere, set EMBEDDINGS_MODEL_DIR to it, run scripts/embeddings_build.py once, set EMBEDDINGS_ENABLED=true and
# restart. The model is about 470 MB on disk and about 0.5 GB of memory when loaded. EMBEDDINGS_DIR is where the vectors are kept (default backend/data/embeddings; keep it out of a cloud-synced folder).
EMBEDDINGS_ENABLED=false
EMBEDDINGS_MODEL_DIR=
EMBEDDINGS_DIR=
# Re-ranker for meaning-based search (lib/embeddings.py): OFF by default and needs EMBEDDINGS_ENABLED too. It re-orders the first 10 results only. Model: BAAI/bge-reranker-v2-m3 (Apache-2.0), the ONNX int8 file
# from onnx-community/bge-reranker-v2-m3-ONNX (about 570 MB; needs onnx/model_int8.onnx, tokenizer.json and tokenizer_config.json). About 2 s per search on a laptop CPU.
RERANKER_ENABLED=false
RERANKER_MODEL_DIR=
# Meaning-based choice of passages from a matter's documents in Research (lib/matter_meaning.py): OFF by default; needs EMBEDDINGS_ENABLED and the model too. It runs the model over
# client documents on this machine only; nothing is stored or sent. Adds about 5 to 12 seconds to the FIRST question on a large matter (later questions are quick).
EMBEDDINGS_MATTER_ENABLED=false
# Word / Google Docs add-ins (addins/README.md): days an add-in key for the Google Docs add-on stays valid (1 to 90, default 30).
ADDIN_KEY_DAYS=30
# --- Optional yearly plan: offered only when these are set (no price is ever assumed). Same currency as PRO_PRICE_AMOUNT; PayPal bills in US dollars.
# PRO_PRICE_YEARLY_AMOUNT=
# PRO_PRICE_USD_YEARLY=
# --- Optional local OCR. If the Tesseract program is installed (with English, Telugu and Hindi language data) VIDHI reads scanned pages with it first and records its real confidence; otherwise scans go to the hosted AI reader. Set the full path if it is not on the PATH. Not benchmarked yet: scripts/ocr_benchmark.py.
# TESSERACT_CMD=
# --- Optional local model (Ollama). Used ONLY for low-risk tasks (question translation for search, simple classification); never for research, document analysis or notices. No per-token fee; you pay in hardware and power. Not evaluated yet (docs/VIDHI_COST_MODEL.md).
# OLLAMA_URL=http://127.0.0.1:11434
# OLLAMA_MODEL=
# AI_LOCAL_TASKS_FIRST=false
# --- Longest scanned PDF read automatically, in pages (a cost limit)
# OCR_MAX_PAGES=60
# OCR_LANGUAGES=eng+tel+hin   (add +tam for Tamil only after measuring on real scans: on 12 synthetic images four languages at once read Telugu slightly worse)

# Optional book library (philosophy, history, science readings). false = book search returns nothing and analyses cite no books; the legal library is separate and unaffected.
KNOWLEDGE_ENABLED=true

# Authority Check (off until you switch it on). Cases are read from the local Supreme Court dataset (SC_DATA_DIR below); no key is needed for that.
AUTHORITY_CHECK_ENABLED=false
# List of dates with page references (off until you switch it on). No AI, no outside service, no cost.
DATE_LIST_ENABLED=false
# Pre-filing defect check (off until you switch it on). Points to drafting slips only; it knows no court's rules. No AI, no outside service, no cost.
DEFECT_CHECK_ENABLED=false
# Old-code to new-code checker (off until you switch it on). Lists where a draft names the IPC, CrPC or Evidence Act; a newer section is shown only from a reviewed mapping. No AI, no outside service, no cost.
OLD_CODE_CHECK_ENABLED=false
# Deadline engine (off until you switch it on). Works out a date only from a rule a named reviewer has marked reviewed; the code contains no law. No AI, no outside service, no cost.
DEADLINE_ENGINE_ENABLED=false
# How many days a Toolkit report is kept before it is deleted automatically (1 to 3650; anything else means 30). The reports hold sentences from a client's draft.
TOOLKIT_REPORT_DAYS=30
AUTHORITY_DAILY_LOOKUP_CAP=300
AUTHORITY_COST_PER_LOOKUP_INR=0.7
# Test scripts set this to true so no test ever calls the paid case source, whatever tokens backend/.env holds. Leave unset in production.
AUTHORITY_SOURCE_DISABLED=false

# --- Pilot access (decision D6) ---
# open = anyone can create an account (the default). invite = a NEW account needs an invitation made in the admin console for that exact email address. Signing in is never affected.
SIGNUP_MODE=open

# --- Backups: encryption needs GnuPG (gpg). Set GPG_BIN only if gpg is not on the PATH (a Windows laptop, for example). ---
GPG_BIN=

# --- Case source for Authority Check ---
# Folder holding the Supreme Court open dataset made by scripts/opendata_download.py (judgments 1950 to date, CC-BY-4.0, free, no key). Empty = no case source: every case then reads "could not check".
SC_DATA_DIR=

# --- Data kept for a limited time (decision D5) ---
# Uploaded documents are deleted this many days after upload (owners are emailed 7 days before). Empty or 0 = off. The pilot uses 30. Allowed: 8 to 365.
UPLOAD_MAX_DAYS=

# --- Law and judgment data ---
# Folder of High Court / Supreme Court sample judgment files (default: backend/data/hc_judgments). The bulk case list lives in the database.
HC_JUDGMENTS_DIR=
# Where the Tantivy search index over the court case list lives (several gigabytes; rebuild with scripts/judgment_index_build.py). Keep it out of a cloud-synced folder. Empty = backend/data/judgment_index.
JUDGMENT_INDEX_DIR=
# Where the paragraph index over stored judgment text lives (rebuild with scripts/passage_index_build.py; about 14 KB per judgment that has text). Not used by the app yet. Empty = backend/data/passage_index.
PASSAGE_INDEX_DIR=
# The plans (free, pro, firm): AI requests a day, how much the AI reads at once, locked tasks, how many people, prices. A JSON file the operator edits, picked up within seconds with no restart. Empty = backend/data/plans.json. A file with a mistake is ignored as a whole (built-in defaults used). FREE_AI_PER_DAY, PRO_AI_PER_DAY, FREE_CONTEXT_CHARS and FREE_AI_PLATFORM_PER_DAY, when set, still win over the file.
PLANS_FILE=
# Law drafts taken from India Code stay switched off until written permission is recorded here (who gave it, and when). Leave empty if there is none; never invent a value.
INDIA_CODE_PERMISSION_REF=
# The Ministry of Home Affairs portal text (BNS, BNSS, BSA from the NCRB Sankalan pages) has its own switch, so it can be on while India Code stays off. Write who decided and when; never invent a value.
NCRB_PORTAL_USE_REF=
# Switch for only the three repealed codes (IPC 1860, CrPC 1973, Evidence Act 1872) taken from India Code files: needed so old-code to new-code mappings can name the old sections. Write who decided and when; never invent a value.
OLD_CODES_USE_REF=
# Acts from other official sites (read 2026-11-18, terms NOT read): each stays switched off until you write down what that site's terms allow (who decided, and when). Never invent a value.
# CBIC (GST Acts), SEBI, the Ministry of Labour and Employment, the Central Information Commission (RTI), the Competition Commission, IP India (Patents). See docs/legal-sources-terms.md.
CBIC_USE_REF=
SEBI_USE_REF=
LABOUR_MINISTRY_USE_REF=
CIC_USE_REF=
CCI_USE_REF=
IPINDIA_USE_REF=

# Optional OCR: a folder holding extra Tesseract language files (hin, tel, tam, ...) plus a copy of the install configs folder. Languages to read: OCR_LANGUAGES above.
# OCR_TESSDATA_DIR=

# Optional virus scan of every upload through ClamAV (clamd). MALWARE_SCAN = off (default), on (scan; allow if the scanner is down) or required (refuse if the scanner is down).
# MALWARE_SCAN=off
# CLAMD_HOST=127.0.0.1
# CLAMD_PORT=3310
